{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots."}]},{"code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The diagram of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true.","type":"text"}]},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertex","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Low child"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High child"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"root"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"false","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"true","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"type":"text","text":" is shared: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"},{"type":"text","text":" false and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1"},{"type":"text","text":" both leave "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" equal to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"type":"text","text":", so both lead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the one vertex that stands for it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" in O(|","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"f","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"| |","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"g","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"|), through a computed table of results","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already found. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" fixes a variable, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" quantify","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a table of families of sets (Minato, 1993). Its vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test elements in index order, with a low child for the sets without the element and a high child"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for those with it. In place of the rule that removes a vertex with equal children, it removes one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose high child is the empty family, so an element no set contains never appears in a diagram,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a sparse family over many elements stays small."}]},{"code":["var diagram = ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram(elementCount: 3)","let f = diagram.family([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2]])","diagram.count(of: f)                                 \/\/ 3","diagram.minimalSets(of: diagram.including(2, in: f)) \/\/ {{2}}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Families combine by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/union(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/intersection(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/subtracting(_:from:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and set by set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/join(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/meet(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/setsView(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists a family’s sets, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" like the binary diagram’s."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"title":"DecisionDiagrams","externalID":"DecisionDiagrams"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Canonical diagrams of Boolean functions and families of sets."}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Binary decision diagrams","anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"]},{"title":"Zero-suppressed decision diagrams","anchor":"Zero-suppressed-decision-diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"]}],"references":{"doc://DecisionDiagrams/documentation/DecisionDiagrams/BinaryDecisionDiagram/graphView-swift.property":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"graphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16DecisionDiagrams06BinaryA7DiagramV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16DecisionDiagrams06BinaryA7DiagramV9GraphViewV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams\/binarydecisiondiagram\/graphview-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The table’s vertices as a directed acyclic graph: a vertex per diagram vertex, 0 the false"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant and 1 the true one, and from each other vertex a low edge and a high edge, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\